        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_984577415.1",
        "comments": "The assembly drAcePsed1.hap1.1 is based on 32x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The assembly resolves into 26 clear homologous chromosome pairs, submitted as haplotype 1 and haplotype 2. Additional homology between chromosome pairs is consistent with allotetraploidy. The exact order and orientation of the scaffolds on chromosome 6 (1 ? 5,700 Kbp) are uncertain. The exact order and orientation of the scaffolds on chromosome 11 (1 ? 4,891 Kbp) are uncertain. The exact order and orientation of the scaffolds on chromosome 22 (30,716 ? 36,263 Kbp) are uncertain. A haplotypic inversion was observed in the region on chromosome 5 (23,263 ? 39,344 Kbp). A haplotypic inversion was observed in the region on chromosome 11 (32,141 ? 36,860 & 36,879 ? 40,827 Kbp).\nA haplotypic inversion was observed in the region on chromosome 12 (4,564 ? 13,037 & 13,268 ? 28,136 & 36,783 ? 40,268 Kbp).",
